{"title":"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many more coins does it take to make one dollar (100) using only nickels(5 coins) than it takes to make one dollar using only dimes(10 coins)?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/9/d492fdbf768c3a4bf8f8a6967278b7870d39b801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\  15\\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 10\\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 75\\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 64\\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 54$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since a dollar is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> cents and a nickel is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cents, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c2c44ceed8d0e53d16cfebfe57436fb7e83b0e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{100}{5} = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" /> nickels in a dollar.\n</p><p>Using this logic for dimes and the fact that a dime is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cents, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/a/4faac259fbbb9a2bbd3462a74dfe39c57d0a3237.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{100}{10} = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" /> dimes in a dollar.\n</p><p>Thus, it takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/0/6204ccb71a2d47be8161a04690de0ed1bc204f6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 - 10 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"149\" height=\"30\" /> more coins to make a dollar using only nickels than it takes to make one dollar using only dimes.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_P